WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.466
(gentle upbeat music)

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.100
- Hi, this is Lindsay Rose
Medoff from Suay Sew Shop,

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.240
and here are three ways to
fight fashion waste at home.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.070
Number one, loving your
clothes make them last.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.190
We're always taught

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:04.680
to not have a sentimental
attachment to clothing,

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.270
but we need to be more attached
to the things that we buy

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:09.550
'cause those items took natural resources

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:10.750
and labor to create.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.230
The longer you hold onto things,

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:14.940
the less of an impact it's
gonna have on the environment.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.850
Number two, mending matters.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:18.320
Every time you patch your clothes

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.770
instead of throwing them in the trash,

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.650
that's gonna extend the life of them

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.520
and reduce the impact on the planet.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.140
Number three is to share
your sustainability story.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.200
Tell your friends and
family what you're up to.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.240
Tell them about choosing used,
recycling, remade, upcycling.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.620
Tell them that there are other options

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.440
besides buying brand-new clothing.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.910
The only way that we're gonna
make massive positive change

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.973
on the planet, is by doing it together.

00:01:40.942 --> 00:01:44.942
(gentle upbeat music continues)

